"""The portal: portalr's two UIs and its router, over the same grantr as the libraries'.

- ``/portalr/app/``: the app, where people chat with the agents and see their work
- ``/portalr/admin/``: the admin, for a tenant's owners and admins, and the deployment's operators
- ``/portalr/v1``: the reads behind them: traces, logs, metrics, scores and spend, each asked of
  grantr first, for the caller's tenant
- ``/auth/v1/token``, ``/auth/v1/user`` and ``/auth/v1/logout``: Supabase Auth's three calls the
  UIs sign in with, passed on, where ``PORTAL_SUPABASE_URL`` is ``/``, this origin

On its own origin, the portal signs in wherever the application is reached: on this machine, on
a tailnet (``make tailnet``), or behind a proxy, with GoTrue alone or Supabase's gateway behind
it. The calls go where the deployment's commands find people, ``AUTH_ADMIN_URL`` or
``AUTH_ISSUER``; only those three, and nothing of the admin API. Reached at more than one origin,
``PORTAL_URL`` and ``PORTAL_EXTRA_URLS``, it runs mini apps and opens the editors at each, beside
it on their own ports (portalr ADR-0084).

It is mounted only where the Supabase project the UIs sign in to is named (``PORTAL_SUPABASE_URL``
and ``PORTAL_SUPABASE_KEY``); a tool is read only where its address is. The Supabase secret key
stays here, for inviting people and naming them by email, and is never in what the browser is given.
"""

